<title>SWITZERLAND: FORECAST - Institute KOF details Swiss forecasts.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Institute KOF details Swiss forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss economic research institute KOF published the following details of its autumn economic forecast for Switzerland.</p>
<p>Prices from 1980 and percentage change from previous year (unless otherwise indicated):</p>
<p>						1996     1997     1998</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product (GDP)	 -0.4     +0.9     +1.9</p>
<p> Private consumption		    +0.5     +0.6     +1.2</p>
<p> Public consumption		     +0.1     -1.8     +0.2</p>
<p> Capital investments		    +0.5     -0.1     +0.9</p>
<p> Construction investments	     -3.6     -1.7     +1.5</p>
<p> Machinery, equipment investments   +6.6     +2.0     +0.2</p>
<p> Exports of goods and services	+2.0     +3.6     +5.2</p>
<p> Imports of goods and services	+1.7     +2.8     +3.5</p>
<p> Changes in stock			 -0.9     +0.6     +0.3</p>
<p> Three-month Eurofrancs		 +2.0     +2.4     +2.8</p>
<p> Avg yield on federal debt (level)  +4.1     +4.3     +4.5</p>
<p> Consumer prices			  +0.8     +1.0     +1.8</p>
<p>Unemployment rate (percentage</p>
<p>    of labour force)		    +4.6     +5.0     +5.0</p>
<p> Real, external value of franc	-2.0     -1.5     -0.3</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
